Build 85 - The Golden Bough Uber Reworked: Akremon, the Grasping Root

The uber at the Golden Bough forecourt is no longer a near-clone of the base-game
Charon. The same shrine and the same walk now lead to an entirely new two-phase fight.

Phase 1, Akremon the Grasping Root: a colossal black tree with every hand that ever
reached for the Bough grown into it. It is BLEED-IMMUNE (park the bleed spears), roots
you in place, and grows a living wall of quillvines between you and it - the only
monster in the mod that builds terrain. At one third life the bark splits, the thorns
come out, and it hits 35 percent harder, with no damage shield and no self-heal, so it
gets more dangerous without getting less killable.

Phase 2, Akremon the Heartwood Ablaze: the burning heartwood walks out of the trunk,
faster, on fire, and NOT bleed-immune - the build you shelved gets the kill. Two
Handbriar champions whip alongside.

The tree is weak to fire and cold; the thing that comes out of it resists fire. Both
forms are resistant but not immune to stun, freeze and traps. Tuned to 35,000 life on
Epic across both forms, matched to Alkyoneus the Soul-Gaoler: it should be hard, and it
should die.

Rewards are unchanged in kind: THE GOLDEN BOUGH amulet (guaranteed), the Soul of the
Grasping Root (grants Graft the Burning Heartwood, a permanent burning cutting that
fights for you and roots what you strike, for a little movement speed), the hoard chest
now called The Orchard of Hands, and the boss orb.

Under the hood: database plus text only, no map change. Existing characters and saves
are unaffected. Names are provisional and may change.
